    "caption": "This is not modesty. It's how the product works.\n\nGoogle Maps results are **personalised by the searcher's distance from your business.** Someone standing 200 m away and someone 5 km away see a different order. There is no single \"position 1\" that exists to be sold to you.\n\nSo what can honestly be promised?\n\n✓ A measured baseline before anything changes\n✓ Category and attribute work reverse-engineered from who's actually ranking\n✓ NAP consistency fixed across the directories that matter\n✓ A review-asking system your staff actually use\n✓ Your website's structured data matching your profile exactly\n✓ A monthly report showing what moved, against that baseline\n\nMovement usually shows in 30–60 days. Competitive urban categories take 3–6 months of sustained work.\n\nAnyone quoting you a fixed date and a fixed position is guessing, and charging you for the guess.",
