    "hook": "Ask your developer one question: \"who owns the code?\" Watch the pause.",
    "script": "(0–6s) \"One question that tells you everything about your software vendor: who owns the code?\"\n(6–15s) \"If it's in *their* GitHub, on *their* server, with *their* domain registrar — you don't own software. You're renting it, and the rent can change.\"\n(15–24s) \"Ours goes in your Git organisation from the first commit. Deploys to your accounts. Handover includes environment variables, a seed script and a runbook.\"\n(24–30s) \"That means you can fire us and keep everything. That's not generosity. It just means we have to keep earning it.\"",
    "caption": "The test: if you hired an in-house developer tomorrow, could they take over without calling your current vendor?\n\nIf the answer is no, that isn't a technical situation. It's a commercial one, and it was designed.\n\nAsk the question. Whatever the answer, you'll know where you stand.",
