    "hook": "Same medicine. Three batches. Three expiry dates. Three MRPs.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Why \"just use billing software\" fails in a pharmacy, in one example.\n\nYour software says: **Paracetamol 500 — 240 units.**\n\nThe shelf says:\n📦 Batch A — 80 units — expires in 3 months — MRP ₹22\n📦 Batch B — 60 units — expires in 14 months — MRP ₹24\n📦 Batch C — 100 units — expires in 26 months — MRP ₹24\n\nIf the counter sells Batch C first because it's at the front, Batch A becomes a write-off — discovered at stock-taking, after the supplier's return window closed.\n\n**First-expiry-first-out at the point of billing** solves it, and it can only exist if the data model knows about batches at all. You can't add it later with a report.\n\nThat's the whole argument for custom, in one shelf.",
