    "hook": "What does one finished unit cost you? Not the estimate. The number.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "For factories, fabricators and job-work units:\n\nMost owners can quote a cost per unit instantly. Almost none can show where the number comes from.\n\nBecause it's usually: raw material at last purchase rate + a labour figure that hasn't changed in two years + \"overheads\" as a percentage somebody picked.\n\n**What actual costing needs:**\n🔩 Bill of materials with multi-level assemblies\n📋 Work orders and job cards, machine-wise\n⚖️ Raw material issued vs actually consumed vs wasted\n🔍 Batch and lot traceability, input to dispatch\n💰 Cost computed from what was really used on that job\n\nThe gap between the estimate and the actual is where your margin is going. And you can't see it because nothing records it as it happens.",
