    "title": "Migration is the job",
    "hook": "The software wasn't the hard part. Getting 8 years of records into it was.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Every ERP rollout that fails, fails at the same place. Not the build — the migration.\n\nBecause the opening data has to be **trustworthy on day one**, or nobody believes any number the system shows afterwards, and they quietly keep the old register \"just to be safe\". Six months later the register is still the real system.\n\n**How we do it:**\n1. Map your existing columns to the new model, in writing\n2. Import into a staging environment first\n3. **Reconcile against a physical count** before go-live — not against the old file, against reality\n4. Fix the gaps while the old system is still running\n5. Only then switch\n\nAnd the paper register stays until it's provably redundant. We don't take it away on day one to force adoption. That's how you get staff keeping a *third* secret system.\n\nMigration and training are part of the rollout. Not an add-on.",
