    "caption": "Off-the-shelf tools fail for the same reason every time, and it isn't quality.\n\nThey enforce a sales process that isn't yours. So your team keeps a private spreadsheet alongside it. Within a quarter the spreadsheet is the real system and the software is a licence fee.\n\n**Narrow beats broad** when narrow matches reality:\n→ The 12 things your team actually does\n→ The stages they name out loud, including the awkward ones\n→ The fields they'd actually fill in\n→ Nothing they don't need\n\nThat's a smaller, cheaper, less impressive-sounding project. It's also the one that survives contact with a Monday morning.\n\nIf your process IS standard — genuinely standard — buy the off-the-shelf tool. We'll name it for you.",
