    "hook": "The one CRM feature that decides whether it gets used.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Not the dashboard. Not the mobile app. **Stage-gated required fields.**\n\nHere's what it means. A deal cannot move from \"quoted\" to \"negotiating\" until the quote amount and the decision-maker's name are filled in. Not a reminder — the system won't let it.\n\nWhy it matters: every CRM that fails, fails the same way. Reps skip fields because nothing forces them, the data becomes 40% complete, the reports become useless, and within a quarter everyone's back on a private spreadsheet.\n\nThe fix isn't discipline. It's making the next stage impossible without the information the next stage depends on.\n\nAsk your CRM vendor whether they can enforce fields per stage. Most can't.",
