    "title": "The problem",
    "hook": "Count one shelf. Then check the software. Do they match?",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "The fastest audit of your operations, and it takes ten minutes.\n\nPick one fast-moving item. Count it physically. Open the system. Compare.\n\n**If they match** — good, your operations layer is working.\n**If they don't** — that gap didn't appear today. It's been growing for months, and every purchase decision you've made in that time used the wrong number.\n\nThe usual causes, in order:\n1. Returns and damages not recorded\n2. Internal consumption not recorded\n3. Two people editing the same sheet\n4. Stock granularity that doesn't match reality — batches, variants, units\n\nNumber 4 is the one nobody fixes, because fixing it means changing the data model, not the process.\n\nTry the count. Post what you find.",
    "hashtags": "#GSTBilling #BillingSoftware #SoftwareDevelopment #DehradunBusiness #BusinessOwner",
    "imagePrompt": "Still life of a warehouse stock register book open on a metal shelf edge, pencil resting in the gutter, boxes softly out of focus behind, one orange inventory tag clipped to the shelf. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
