    "format": "Archetype F",
    "title": "How it works",
    "hook": "Generic software thinks a medicine is one product. It isn't.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Why \"just use billing software\" fails, in one shelf.\n\nYour software says: **Paracetamol 500 — 240 units.**\n\nThe shelf says:\n📦 Batch A — 80 units — expires in 3 months — MRP ₹22\n📦 Batch B — 60 units — expires in 14 months — MRP ₹24\n📦 Batch C — 100 units — expires in 26 months — MRP ₹24\n\nIf the counter sells Batch C first because it's at the front, Batch A becomes a write-off — discovered at stock-taking, after the supplier's return window closed.\n\n**First-expiry-first-out at the point of billing** fixes it, and it can only exist if the data model knows about batches at all. You can't add it later with a report.\n\nThat's the whole argument for custom, in one shelf.",
    "hashtags": "#ERPSoftware #InventoryManagement #BusinessSoftware #Dehradun #SmallBusinessIndia",
    "imagePrompt": "Blueprint schematic on warm paper of three stacked horizontal bars with different lengths and thin orange annotation arrows pointing to the shortest, technical drafting style, faint grid, measurement marks. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
    "day": 0,
