    "title": "Myth-buster",
    "hook": "The ERP rollout doesn't fail at the build. It fails at the migration.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Every one we've seen go wrong, went wrong in the same place.\n\nBecause the opening data has to be **trustworthy on day one**, or nobody believes any number the system shows afterwards — and they quietly keep the old register \"just to be safe\". Six months later the register is still the real system.\n\n**How it should be done:**\n1. Map your existing columns to the new model, in writing\n2. Import into a staging environment first\n3. **Reconcile against a physical count** before go-live — against reality, not against the old file\n4. Fix the gaps while the old system still runs\n5. Only then switch\n\nAnd the paper register stays until it's provably redundant. Taking it away on day one to force adoption is how you get staff keeping a *third* secret system.\n\nMigration and training are part of the rollout. Not an add-on.",
    "hashtags": "#GSTBilling #BillingSoftware #SoftwareDevelopment #Uttarakhand #MSME",
    "imagePrompt": "Extreme macro of the edge of a stack of old ledger paper on warm paper, the top sheet lifting slightly, one orange bookmark ribbon threading through, shallow depth of field. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
    "day": 0,
    "order": 81
