    "hook": "30+ reports. The client asked for exactly zero of them upfront.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Here's how a reports list should actually get made.\n\nNot from a requirements document. From standing next to the operators for a week and writing down every question they asked out loud each morning.\n\n\"How much did we do yesterday?\"\n\"Which attendant had the shortfall?\"\n\"Who's over their credit limit?\"\n\"What's outstanding older than 30 days?\"\n\nThirty-plus reports came out of that. Every one gets opened, because every one answers a question somebody was already asking.\n\nThe alternative — forty charts built from a spec — produces a dashboard people screenshot once and never revisit.\n\n**Want to know what we'd build for you? First tell us what you ask out loud every morning.**",
