    "title": "Who it's for",
    "hook": "Five questions. Every \"no\" costs you an hour a month, forever.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "❓ Does the total in your billing software match what hit the bank?\n❓ Can you list who's over their credit limit right now, without asking anyone?\n❓ Do part-payments show against the right invoice automatically?\n❓ Is receivables ageing something you *look at*, or something you *compile*?\n❓ Does a credit note reverse GST correctly, or does someone fix it by hand?\n\nEvery \"no\" isn't a small annoyance. It's an hour a month, forever, plus the risk that a genuine problem hides inside a routine discrepancy.\n\nCredit limits enforced **at the point of sale** rather than reviewed monthly is the single highest-leverage fix on that list. It stops the problem instead of reporting it.",
