    "hook": "A customer paid twice. The gateway says once. Who's wrong?",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "This is the bug almost every first build has, and it's invisible until it costs you.\n\n**How it breaks:** the browser redirects back after payment, and *that redirect* creates the order. If the customer's network drops at that moment — or they refresh — the order either never gets created, or gets created twice.\n\n**How it should work:** the order is created from the gateway's own server-to-server webhook, with an idempotency key. Same payment fires the webhook five times? Exactly one order. Customer closes the tab mid-payment? The order still lands.\n\nAsk whoever built your system one question: *\"is the order created from the redirect or from the webhook?\"*\n\nTheir answer tells you everything.",
