    "hook": "A ₹4,000 shortfall. Nobody knows which shift it came from.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Fuel retail reconciles in a way no standard billing module expects: dip readings vs nozzle totalisers vs cash collected vs credit issued. Per shift. Per attendant.\n\nAcross three sites, this happened on paper the following morning — by which point nobody could say which shift a shortfall belonged to. So it became an argument instead of a number.\n\n**What we built:** nozzle-level entry capturing opening and closing totaliser readings, tank dips and density, reconciled against cash, card and credit at shift close.\n\nMeaning the variance is attributed **while the attendant is still on site.**\n\nCredit customers carry limits enforced at the point of sale, not reviewed monthly. 30+ reports built from what operators actually asked each morning.\n\n3 sites live. Not a percentage — a different Monday.",
