    "title": "How it works",
    "hook": "The confidence gate — the part that makes automation safe.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Invoices land in a watched inbox and get parsed to structured line items. Then the important bit.\n\n**High confidence** → written straight through.\n**Below the threshold** → a scanned copy, an unusual layout, a smudged total → goes to a review queue where one click confirms or corrects it.\n\nThat threshold is the whole design. Without it you have a system that's right most of the time and silently wrong the rest — which is worse than doing it by hand, because nobody's checking.\n\nAccuracy is logged per supplier. Drift raises an alert instead of quietly corrupting a quarter of data.\n\n**Ask any automation vendor: what happens when it isn't sure?** If they don't have an answer, they haven't built one.",
    "hashtags": "#AIAutomation #WorkflowAutomation #BusinessSoftware #Dehradun #SmallBusinessIndia",
    "imagePrompt": "Abstract composition of a stream of small geometric shapes flowing toward a threshold line, most continuing through in orange and a few diverting sideways in grey, soft gradients, generous empty space above. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
