    "hook": "The register stayed on the counter for four months. On purpose.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Nobody tells you this part.\n\nWhen we digitise an operation, the paper register does not leave on go-live day. It sits beside the terminal, and for a few weeks the team writes in both.\n\nThat looks like waste. It's the opposite: it's the only way staff find out for themselves that the software has the number they need, faster than the book does.\n\nThe day they stop reaching for it is the day the rollout actually succeeded — and it's their decision, not ours.\n\nTake the register away early and you don't get adoption. You get a third secret system.",
