    "title": "How it works",
    "hook": "One field on your profile matters more than all the others.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Your **primary category**.\n\nIt decides which searches you're eligible to appear for at all. Get it wrong and no volume of reviews, photos or posts will fix it — you're competing in the wrong race.\n\n**The mistake:** picking the category that describes what you *are*.\n**The fix:** picking the one that matches what customers *search*.\n\n→ \"Ayurvedic clinic\" vs **\"Ayurveda practitioner\"** vs **\"Alternative medicine practitioner\"**\n→ \"Computer shop\" vs **\"Computer repair service\"** vs **\"Computer store\"**\n→ \"Tiffin service\" vs **\"Meal delivery\"** vs **\"Caterer\"**\n\nEach pulls a completely different set of searches, with different competition.\n\n**How to actually choose it:** search your main keyword, open the top three listings in the map pack, check what category *they* use. That's reverse-engineering what Google has already decided works.\n\nThen set up to 9 secondary categories. Almost nobody does, and it's free.",
