    "hook": "A technician in a lift shaft finishes the job. The sync is our problem.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "\"Offline support\" usually means the app shows an error and loses what you typed. Here's what it should mean.\n\n**Every write goes to a local queue first.** The app doesn't wait for the network — it saves locally, confirms to the user, and reconciles server-side when signal returns.\n\n**Conflict rules are agreed in scope, before code.** What happens if two people edited the same job offline? That's a decision, not an accident.\n\n**Nothing is ever lost mid-form.** Ever.\n\nWhere this matters: basements, lift shafts, stairwells, warehouses, rural routes, construction sites, godowns with metal roofs.\n\nWhich is to say: almost everywhere real work happens.",
    "hashtags": "#AppDevelopment #FieldService #SoftwareDevelopment #DehradunBusiness #BusinessOwner",
    "imagePrompt": "Abstract composition of small geometric blocks stacking into a vertical queue, the lower ones grey and the top one vivid orange, with a faint dotted line rising away, soft gradients, generous empty space above. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
