    "title": "Myth-buster",
    "hook": "Most businesses asking for an app don't need one. Here's the test.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "We get asked for an app about twice a week. Maybe a third actually need one.\n\n**You need a real app if you need any of these:**\n✓ Working offline — a technician in a basement, a driver with no signal\n✓ Push notifications that arrive when the app is closed\n✓ Background location or live tracking\n✓ Camera, barcode or hardware access\n✓ Something people open every single day\n\n**You don't if:**\n✗ It's a catalogue people browse occasionally\n✗ It's a form\n✗ \"Our competitor has one\"\n✗ You just want to be on the Play Store\n\nIf none of the first list applies, a fast mobile website does the same job for a third of the cost, updates instantly, and needs nobody to install anything.\n\nWe'll tell you which on the first call. Yes, even when it means a smaller project.",
    "hashtags": "#IOSApp #MobileAppDevelopment #StartupIndia #IndiaBusiness #Entrepreneur",
    "imagePrompt": "Extreme macro of a phone screen edge and bezel against warm paper, dust visible in the raking light, screen dark and reflective, one orange reflection along the rim, very shallow depth of field. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
