    "hook": "Lose these two files and you can't update your own app.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "The Android keystore and the Apple signing credentials.\n\nWithout them you cannot publish an update. The only remedy is creating a **new** store listing and asking every existing user to find and reinstall it — which loses your ratings, your install base and your review history.\n\nDevelopers hold these more often than you'd think. Sometimes deliberately. Usually just carelessly.\n\n**Ask before the project starts:**\n→ Whose name is the Play Console account in?\n→ Whose name is the Apple Developer account in?\n→ Where will the keystore live, and who has a copy?\n\nOurs go in your business's name, and the keys are handed to you at release. That means you can fire us and keep shipping — which is exactly the leverage a client should have.",
    "hashtags": "#ReactNative #AndroidApp #CustomSoftware #Dehradun #SmallBusinessIndia",
    "imagePrompt": "Still life of two small brass keys on a plain warm paper surface, one slightly overlapping the other, a single orange tag looped through one key, overhead, hard directional light, deep shadow. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
