    "title": "Who it's for",
    "hook": "Staff app or customer app? They're different products.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "People say \"we need an app\" meaning one of two completely different things.\n\n**A staff app** is a tool. Used daily, by people you train, on devices you can specify. Success = fewer phone calls and faster paperwork. Offline matters enormously. Design can be plain.\n\n**A customer app** is a product. Used occasionally, by people you can't train, on devices you can't control. Success = they install it and come back. Design matters enormously. Getting installs is harder than building it.\n\n**The uncomfortable one:** most businesses asking for a customer app would do better with a fast mobile website. Nobody installs an app for a service they use four times a year.\n\nStaff apps almost always pay back. Customer apps need a reason to be reopened.",
    "hashtags": "#AppDevelopment #FieldService #BusinessAdvice #Uttarakhand #MSME",
    "imagePrompt": "Blueprint schematic on warm paper of two parallel columns of stacked screen wireframes, the left column traced in vivid orange and the right in grey, drafting annotation style, faint grid. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
