    "title": "The problem",
    "hook": "Orders from three places. Stock in one spreadsheet. Something oversold.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Selling online breaks in a predictable place — not the storefront, the second channel.\n\nThe moment orders arrive from a website, a marketplace and Instagram at once, inventory becomes three people editing one sheet, and something oversells.\n\nOverselling on a marketplace costs a metric that's hard to repair. And it's never the fault of the person who made the mistake — it's the fault of an architecture where three systems each believe they own the stock number.\n\n**One ledger. Every channel writes to it.** That's the whole fix, and it has to be built in rather than added after the first incident.\n\nHow many places hold your stock count right now? 👇",
    "hashtags": "#SellOnline #OrderManagement #BusinessSoftware #DehradunBusiness #BusinessOwner",
    "imagePrompt": "Still life of three small cardboard shipping boxes on warm paper, each with a different faint handwritten marking, one box tipped and slightly open, a single orange packing tape strip across it, overhead. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
