    "title": "Myth-buster",
    "hook": "Shopify vs custom. Do the arithmetic, not the argument.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "We'll recommend Shopify to your face when it's right. Here's how to tell.\n\n**Shopify wins when:**\n✓ Straightforward retail catalogue, one price per product\n✓ You want it live next week\n✓ You don't have an ERP to sync with\n✓ Volume is low enough that the commission doesn't sting\n\n**Custom wins when:**\n✓ Wholesale slabs, MOQs or customer-specific rates\n✓ Made-to-order or configurable products\n✓ An existing billing/ERP system that must stay in sync\n✓ The monthly commission has grown past what a build costs\n\nThat last one is arithmetic, not opinion. Take your last twelve months of platform fees plus commission and compare it to a one-off build. Sometimes it's obvious. Sometimes it isn't — and then Shopify is the right answer.",
    "hashtags": "#SellOnline #OrderManagement #DigitalTransformation #Uttarakhand #MSME",
    "imagePrompt": "Extreme macro of a brass balance scale pivot on warm paper, slightly tilted, one pan just visible at the frame edge, one orange weight resting on it, shallow depth of field, tactile metal. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
