    "title": "Proof",
    "hook": "The payment bug almost every first store has.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "A customer paid twice. The gateway says once. Who's wrong?\n\n**How it breaks:** the browser redirects back after payment and *that redirect* creates the order. Network drops at that moment — or they refresh — and the order either never gets created, or gets created twice.\n\n**How it should work:** the order is created from the gateway's server-to-server webhook with an idempotency key. Same payment fires the webhook five times? Exactly one order. Customer closes the tab mid-payment? The order still lands.\n\nAsk whoever built your store: *\"is the order created from the redirect or from the webhook?\"*\n\nTheir answer tells you everything, including whether they've ever had to refund someone for this.",
    "hashtags": "#Ecommerce #OnlineStore #BusinessSoftware #DehradunBusiness #BusinessOwner",
    "imagePrompt": "Abstract composition of a looping path that folds back into a single solid endpoint, most of the loop in soft grey with the endpoint in vivid orange, geometric, soft gradients, generous empty space above. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
    "day": 0,
    "order": 118
