    "source": "library",
    "group": "E-commerce & Online Store — from ₹18,000",
    "theme": "Who it's for",
    "slot": "",
    "format": "Archetype D",
    "title": "Who it's for",
    "hook": "Selling on Instagram already? You've outgrown DMs.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "DMs work brilliantly until they don't. The tipping point is specific.\n\n**You've outgrown it when:**\n✓ You're scrolling back through chats to find what someone ordered\n✓ Two people are answering DMs and both promised the last unit\n✓ You're sending UPI QRs manually and matching payments by hand\n✓ Someone asks \"where's my order\" and you check a courier site personally\n\nNone of that means stop selling on Instagram. It means the orders need somewhere to land — one inbox, one stock number, one payment record — with Instagram as a channel into it rather than the system of record.\n\nA chat thread is a conversation. It was never a database.",
    "hashtags": "#EcommerceWebsite #D2C #BusinessTips #IndiaBusiness #Entrepreneur",
    "imagePrompt": "Documentary photograph of a small Indian home business packing table with parcels, tape and a phone propped up, warm afternoon light from the left, one orange parcel in sharp focus, no faces. soft directional daylight from the left, warm paper #ECEAE4 background, one vivid orange #F4501A accent and nothing else saturated, editorial product photography, shot on 50mm, shallow depth of field, generous empty space in the upper third for a text overlay, muted natural palette, photorealistic, 4:5 aspect ratio. no text, no words, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no watermarks, no people looking at camera, no stock-photo handshakes, no clutter, not oversaturated, no HDR, no lens flare.",
    "day": 0,
