    "hook": "Half of all reporting arguments are two people using one word for different numbers.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Does revenue include GST? Is a sale counted at order or at dispatch? Does \"this month\" mean calendar month or your billing cycle? Is a returned item subtracted from the day it sold or the day it came back?\n\nEvery one of those has two defensible answers. Pick one, write it down, and use it everywhere.\n\n**That's the metric dictionary.** It sounds like paperwork and it prevents most of the disputes a reporting system otherwise creates — because when two departments quote different revenue figures, neither is lying. They're using different definitions nobody ever settled.\n\nDefinitions before charts. Always.",
