    "hook": "A number you can't click into is a number you can't trust.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Every figure on the dashboard opens the rows behind it.\n\nSounds minor. It's the difference between a reporting tool people use and one they quietly stop believing.\n\nBecause the first time a number surprises you, you have exactly two options: investigate, or doubt. If you can't click into it, you doubt it. And once you've doubted one number, you doubt all of them — and you're back to asking three people for a figure.\n\nDrill-down isn't a feature. It's what makes the whole thing credible.\n\n**Test any dashboard you're shown: click the biggest number. See what happens.**",
