    "hook": "Have you ever actually restored one of your backups?",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Not \"do you have backups\". Have you restored one.\n\nA backup nobody has ever restored is a rumour. It's the most common form of imaginary safety in small business IT, and you find out it was imaginary on the worst possible day.\n\n**The things that fail quietly:**\n→ A backup job that's been erroring for four months\n→ A restore that works but takes eleven hours nobody budgeted for\n→ A backup of the app but not the database\n→ Credentials to the backup storage that left with someone\n\nWe restore into a scratch environment on a schedule, and the restore *time* goes in your monthly report. Because \"we have backups\" and \"we can be back up in 40 minutes\" are different sentences.\n\nWhen did you last test yours? 👇",
