    "hook": "Patching before the advisory becomes an incident.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "The unglamorous work that decides whether a system quietly keeps running for years.\n\n**What actually happens on a support retainer:**\n→ Dependency advisories monitored, not discovered\n→ Patches applied on a cadence, tested on staging first\n→ Certificates renewed before they expire, not after the site goes red\n→ Disk and memory watched, so \"the server filled up\" isn't a Saturday\n→ Error rates monitored, so a broken form is found by us, not by a lost customer\n\nNone of it shows. All of it is the difference between software that lasts four years and software that becomes \"the thing that keeps breaking\".",
