    "title": "Myth-buster",
    "hook": "\"Response within 24 hours\" isn't a response time. It's a sentence.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "Ask what it means for each severity. If there's one number for everything, it's marketing.\n\n**What written response times look like:**\n→ **Site down:** same working day, out of hours on the higher tier\n→ **Broken but usable:** two working days\n→ **Change request:** inside the monthly allowance, scheduled\n\nIn the agreement. Not implied, not \"we look after our clients\".\n\n**And ask the second question:** what's *excluded*? Ours: cloud infrastructure bills at actuals with no markup, new feature builds, and third-party licences. Written down, so the invoice never surprises you.\n\nA support contract with no severity levels and no exclusions is a hope, not an agreement.",
