    "hook": "Your phone number is different in four places online. Google noticed.",
    "script": "",
    "caption": "NAP = **Name, Address, Phone.** The rule is simple and almost universally broken: it must be **byte-identical everywhere.**\n\nNot similar. Identical.\n\n**Where yours probably differs right now:**\n→ Google Business Profile\n→ Your website footer\n→ Your website's structured data (the part nobody checks)\n→ JustDial, IndiaMART, Sulekha\n→ Your Facebook page\n→ Old directory entries from a vendor you used in 2019\n\n**And these count as different:**\n`Shop 4, MG Road` ≠ `Shop No. 4, M.G. Road`\n`+91 91197 56710` ≠ `9119756710`\n`ABM Tech` ≠ `ABM Tech Solutions`\n\nMismatched details don't merely fail to help. Google treats conflicting information as a signal that the business data is unreliable, and **actively suppresses the listing**. It's one of the most common reasons a good business ranks below a worse one.\n\nA citation sweep is unglamorous, boring work, and it's often the single change that moves a listing.\n\nIncluded in the ₹2,500 setup for the major Indian directories.",
