    "script": "",
    "caption": "The single most common misunderstanding in local SEO, and almost nobody is told it.\n\n**Google ranks a service-area business from the pin on its hidden address** — exactly as it ranks a shop. Listing thirty cities in the service-area field does not make you appear in thirty cities. It tells a customer who has *already found you* what you cover.\n\nSo people list every city within 200 km, see no change, and conclude Maps doesn't work for them.\n\n**What actually moves a service business:**\n✓ Category precision — with no shopfront, this carries more weight\n✓ Review volume and velocity — proximity is fixed, so prominence must do more work\n✓ **Location pages on your own website** — this is where reach beyond the radius comes from\n✓ Address hidden and service areas defined properly, not a home address published\n\nRealistic outcome: you own a radius on Maps, and reach the rest through organic search. Anyone promising city-wide map-pack dominance from one pin is describing something the product doesn't do.\n\n**₹2,500** for correct setup. DM **\"SERVICE AREA\"**.",
