    "script": "",
    "caption": "The instinct is to appeal immediately. It's the wrong move, and it costs you the attempt that matters most.\n\n**An appeal filed on an unchanged profile is refused**, and each refused attempt makes the next one slower.\n\n**The order that works:**\n1. **Diagnose.** Hard suspension (gone from Maps) or soft (still listed, no access)? Different problems.\n2. **Fix the violation** — keywords in the name, an ineligible address, an unsubstantiated category, duplicates, review manipulation\n3. **Assemble documentation** — registration/Udyam, GST certificate, utility bill, rental agreement, exterior signage photos with the street number visible\n4. **File once**, argued properly\n5. **Change nothing** while it's under review\n\nTypical resolution: 3–14 days.\n\n**We can't guarantee reinstatement** — the decision is Google's and nobody controls it. What changes the odds is correct diagnosis, fixing before appealing, and documentation.\n\n**And never create a replacement listing.** It makes a duplicate, compounds the problem, and abandons your reviews permanently.\n\nDM **\"SUSPENDED\"** for a free diagnosis.",
